d put this back in play.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Matt Van Epps (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Matt Van Epps, who won a closely watched December 2025 special election for this seat, seeks a full term against Nashville businessman Darden Copeland, a Democrat. The redrawn district remains strongly Republican, with a partisan lean of about eleven points toward the GOP, and Van Epps holds a large financial edge, including more than $2.4 million in outside support.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the seat Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Van Epps roughly a 95% chance. Copeland ran a competitive primary and has raised a respectable sum, and the special election was tighter than expected, but the structural advantages still favor the incumbent substantially.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0399, "margin": -11.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0725, "margin": -10.5}]}